{%- comment -%}
  THE OASIS — optional phone-specific file for a full-bleed background image

  Wide photographs rarely have an upright crop that works, so every full-bleed
  section can carry a second file shown only on phones.

  <picture> rather than a second <img> hidden with CSS: the browser picks one
  source and downloads that one alone, so a phone never pays for the desktop
  photograph as well.

  The wrapper is `.oasis-bg-picture`, which oasis.css sets to `display: contents`
  so its own box disappears. The <img> therefore stays a direct child of the
  section, and every rule that positions, orders, sizes and crops that section's
  background applies exactly as it does without the wrapper — no parallel set of
  rules per section.

  The media query matches the 989px breakpoint every one of these sections uses
  to stack, so the phone photograph appears exactly when the stacked band does.

  Accepts:
    - image_mobile:   {Image}  optional; when blank this renders `desktop` alone
    - desktop:        {String} the already-rendered <img> for wide screens, so
                               each section keeps its own widths, loading and
                               fetchpriority rather than having them genericised
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if image_mobile != blank -%}
  <picture class="oasis-bg-picture">
    <source
      media="(max-width: 989px)"
      srcset="
        {{ image_mobile | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,
        {{ image_mobile | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,
        {{ image_mobile | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w,
        {{ image_mobile | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w
      "
      sizes="100vw"
      width="{{ image_mobile.width }}"
      height="{{ image_mobile.height }}"
    >
    {{ desktop }}
  </picture>
{%- else -%}
  {{ desktop }}
{%- endif -%}
